Janis Papanagnou <Janis_Papanagnou@hotmail.com> writes:
> Jukka Lahtinen wrote:

> > The way to enter a level with arch-lich before you have magic resistance:
> > Step away from the stairs (the square next to stairs is good).
> > Wait for the L to teleport next to you.
> > Hurt it, so it goes to the stairs to heal itself.
> > Hurt it again when it's on the stairs healing, and it escapes upstairs.

> One logical problem I seem not to be able to grasp with that procedure...
> I shall not meet him without MR if I will follow him up later, but it
> doesn't mind to not have MR while meeting him the first time to hurt him?

The procedure is not absolutely safe, but if you have not found anything
giving MR before entering the castle, it is the way to minimize the risk.
The L often go to the stairs to heal even when they get a minimal wound
that is no way yet dangerous to them. And when you are next to the stairs,
you can usually hit them again before they get completely healed, and
that's when they climb the stairs.
It is *possible* that the arch-lich uses the touch of death before
escaping, but I don't find it very likely when you don't give them too
much time for doing that. This is what I do whenever I am in this
situation. 

